      "name": {
        "name": "Palmitoyltransferase PFA4/ZDHHC16/ZDHHC20/ERF2-like",
        "short": "PFA4/ZDH16/20/ERF2-like"
      },
      "description": [
        {
          "text": "<p>This entry includes palmitoyltransferases such as PFA4, ZDHHC16, ZDHHC20, ERF2 from fungi and its homologues.</p>\n\n<p>PFA4 from S. cerevisiae mediates the reversible addition of palmitate to target proteins, thereby regulating their membrane association and biological function. It palmitoylates several amino acid permeases [[cite:PUB00080267]] and chitin synthase CHS3, which is required for its proper export from the ER [[cite:PUB00079982], [cite:PUB00100513]]. ZDHHC16 is a palmitoyl acyltransferase that mediates palmitoylation of proteins such as PLN and ZDHHC6 [[cite:PUB00090229]]. In zebrafish, there are two ZDHHC16 homologues, ZDHHC16A and ZDHHC16B. They are involved in the proliferation of neural stem cells by regulating the FGF/ERK pathway [[cite:PUB00090230]].</p>\n\n<p>Palmitoyltransferase ZDHHC20 can catalyse the addition of palmitate onto various protein substrates [[cite:PUB00155123], [cite:PUB00155124], [cite:PUB00155027]]. It catalyses the palmitoylation of Cys residues in the cytoplasmic C-terminal of EGFR, and modulates the duration of EGFR signalling by modulating palmitoylation-dependent EGFR internalisation and degradation [[cite:PUB00155123]]. ZDHHC20 can also utilise acyl-CoA with C14 and C18 fatty acid chains [[cite:PUB00155124]].</p>\n\n<p>ERF2 from S. cerevisiae forms a complex with SHR5, palmitoyltransferase specific for Ras proteins. It palmitoylates RAS2, which is required for its proper plasma membrane localisation [[cite:PUB00020585]]. In S. pombe it forms a complex with erf4 complex, a palmitoyltransferase with a major role in driving sexual development [[cite:PUB00044889], [cite:PUB00155125]]. It palmitoylates ras1, isp3 and rho3 [[cite:PUB00155125]].</p>",
          "llm": false,
          "checked": false,
          "updated": false
        }
      ],
